.TH SOCKETPAIR 2
.SH NAME
socketpair \- create a connected AF_UNIX descriptor pair
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/socket.h>
.PP
.B int socketpair(int domain, int type, int protocol, int sv[2]);
.SH DESCRIPTION
socketpair() creates two connected local sockets. Astia accepts AF_UNIX,
SOCK_STREAM, and protocol zero. The two descriptors share a full-duplex
byte stream and do not use a pathname or host networking.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero and stores both descriptors in sv, or returns -1 and sets errno.
Reads block through the native asynchronous I/O ring until data arrives or
the peer closes or shuts down its write side.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EAFNOSUPPORT
The domain is not AF_UNIX or the type is not SOCK_STREAM.
.TP
.B EFAULT
sv is not writable userspace memory.
.TP
.B EMFILE
The process has no room for both descriptors.
.SH NOTES
The descriptor pair is unnamed. Closing either descriptor wakes a blocked
operation on the other descriptor.
